    "text": "For a radioactive material, its activity <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and rate of change of its activity <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are defined as <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> , where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is the number of nuclei at time <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> . Two radioactive sources <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> (mean life <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi></math> ) and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> (mean life <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi></math> ) have the same activity at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> . Their rates of change of activities at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi></math> are <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></msub></math> , respectively. If <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> , then the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> is",
